    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe code reuse is right \u2014 calling `ownerMapper.formatMembershipLevel(owner)` from the controller follows the file's existing precedent (`normalizeTelephone`/`normalizeEmail` are already invoked directly from this same controller, lines 148\u2013149), so no computation is duplicated. The rename is applied coherently across mapper, model/service Javadoc, and openapi.yml. One structural inconsistency:\n\n**`formatMembershipLevel` Javadoc now contradicts its usage, breaking the file's own convention** (`OwnerMapper.java:89\u201390`). The method's Javadoc still reads: *\"`@Named` keeps this out of MapStruct's automatic method selection, so it is applied only where referenced via `qualifiedByName`.\"* But this change introduces a direct call to it from the controller (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:129`), so \"applied only where referenced via `qualifiedByName`\" is now false.\n\nThe codebase already has an established, deliberate pattern for exactly this situation: the two `@Named` helpers that are also called directly \u2014 `normalizeTelephone` (line 163) and `normalizeEmail` (lines 179\u2013180) \u2014 append *\"(and when called directly, e.g. on update)\"* to that sentence. A maintainer would expect `formatMembershipLevel` to match. Update its Javadoc the same way (e.g. \"...via `qualifiedByName` (and when called directly, e.g. to record the membership level on the create audit line)\") so the derivation method's contract stays truthful and consistent with its siblings.",
